Port Flutter's iOS standard edit actions (cut, copy, paste, delete, select all) into gpui_ios.

Ported from flutter/flutter engine/src/flutter/shell/platform/darwin/ios/framework/Source/FlutterTextInputPlugin.mm
@ 3.50.1 (ae9b586f34a8443573f82ef57c3bf914a908cbf7): `-canPerformAction:withSender:` and the
UIResponderStandardEditActions overrides. Copyright 2014 The Flutter Authors. BSD-3-Clause.

What: GPUITextInputView answers `cut:`, `copy:`, `paste:`, `delete:` and `selectAll:` as Flutter's view does, on the
app's text through the input handler, and `canPerformAction:withSender:` with Flutter's rules: paste only when the
pasteboard holds strings (no images or memojis), copy, cut and delete only with selected text, select all only with
text, `captureTextFromCamera:` always. Copy and cut are also off for a secure field: Flutter's framework does that
(`EditableTextState.copyEnabled` / `cutEnabled`), and here UIKit's own edit menu is the field's menu. An action tells
the input delegate around its change, `selectionWillChange:` (and `textWillChange:` unless select all) before and the
`Did` calls after, as UITextInput asks, so UIKit's selection UI follows it. Flutter's view tells it nothing here (its
framework echoes the state back); told only afterwards, UIKit's keyboard collapsed select all's new selection to its
end, since it accepts autocorrection and collapses the selection it knows on `selectionWillChange:`. The view had
none of these: UIKit's edit menu and Cmd+X/C/V/A did nothing in a GPUI field.

Test: patch 0028's rows testStandardEditActions, testCanPerformActionForSelectActions,
testCanPerformActionCaptureTextFromCamera and testPastingNonTextDisallowed move from Open to passing (the last gains
Flutter's "pasteboard holds a colour" step). A Parallax row (not Flutter's) checks the delegate's notices and the
app's selection at each: select all and cut tell it before the selection moves. The oracle binary has no app bundle, so iOS would ask the user before
each general-pasteboard read and hang: under `cfg(test)` the actions use a named pasteboard. Run on the iOS
simulator with `scripts/ios-text-oracle.sh` in Parallax.

Upstream PR: not filed yet.

